ect the incorrect word in the sentence and type the correct form.",sentence:"She doesn't likes to be interrupted during her research.",tokens:["She","doesn't","likes","to","be","interrupted","during","her","research."],incorrectIndex:2,correctAnswers:["like"],explanation:"With auxiliary 'doesn't', base form 'like' is required. 'doesn't likes' is ungrammatical."},{id:"q2",type:"click_correct",question:"Find the error.",sentence:"They was planning to visit the museum yesterday.",tokens:["They","was","planning","to","visit","the","museum","yesterday."],incorrectIndex:1,correctAnswers:["were"],explanation:"Subject-verb agreement: 'They' requires 'were', not 'was'."},{id:"q3",type:"mcq",question:"Choose the correct sentence:",options:{A:"Each of the students have finished.",B:"Each of the students has finished.",C:"Each of the student has finished.",D:"Each students has finished."},correctAnswer:"B",explanation:"'Each' is singular. Correct: Each of the students has finished."}]},"./questions/intermediate/english/reading/question.json":{meta:{title:"Reading Comprehension — Climate",description:"Read passage and answer.",timeLimits:{fast:7,normal:15,easy:25}},questions:[{id:"q1",type:"passage_mcq",passage:"The reversal of ocean currents in the North Atlantic has been linked to abrupt climate shifts. When freshwater influx reduces salinity, density-driven circulation weakens, causing heat transport to stall. Evidence from ice cores suggests such events triggered temperature drops of 5°C within decades.",question:"What weakens density-driven circulation?",options:{A:"Salinity increase",B:"Freshwater influx",C:"Temperature rise",D:"Wind patterns"},correctAnswer:"B",explanation:"Passage states freshwater influx reduces salinity, weakening circulation."},{id:"q2",type:"passage_mcq",passage:"The reversal of ocean currents in the North Atlantic has been linked to abrupt climate shifts. When freshwater influx reduces salinity, density-driven circulation weakens, causing heat transport to stall. Evidence from ice cores suggests such events triggered temperature drops of 5°C within decades.",question:"Ice core evidence indicates:",options:{A:"Gradual warming of 1°C",B:"Sudden drops of 5°C in decades",C:"No correlation with currents",D:"Salinity increase causes warming"},correctAnswer:"B",explanation:"Ice cores show temperature drops of 5°C within decades."},{id:"q3",type:"mcq",question:"Author's tone is:",options:{A:"Speculative but evidence-based",B:"Dismissive",C:"Humorous",D:"Alarmist without data"},correctAnswer:"A",explanation:"Author links hypotheses to ice core evidence."}]},"./questions/advance/math/psychotest/question.json":{meta:{title:"Visual Reasoning & Logic",description:"Image-based reasoning.",timeLimits:{fast:6,normal:12,easy:20}},questions:[{id:"q1",type:"image_mcq",question:"If pattern continues, which completes the sequence? (Visual: ▲ ■ ● → ■ ● ▲ → ? )",image:"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1639322537224-f01285785c00?w=400&h=200&fit=crop",options:{A:"● ▲ ■",B:"▲ ● ■",C:"● ■ ▲",D:"■ ▲ ●"},correctAnswer:"A",explanation:"Rotation: each row shifts left. ▲■● → ■●▲ → ●▲■."},{id:"q2",type:"mcq",question:"What is next: 2, 6, 12, 20, 30, ?",options:{A:"40",B:"42",C:"44",D:"48"},correctAnswer:"B",explanation:"Pattern n*(n+1): 1*2=2, 2*3=6, 3*4=12, 4*5=20, 5*6=30, 6*7=42."}]},"./questions/easy/history/ancient-egypt/question.json":{meta:{title:"Ancient Egypt Basics",description:"Foundational history.",timeLimits:{fast:4,normal:8,easy:15}},questions:[{id:"q1",type:"mcq",question:"Who unified Upper and Lower Egypt?",options:{A:"Tutankhamun",B:"Narmer (Menes)",C:"Ramses II",D:"Cleopatra"},correctAnswer:"B",explanation:"Narmer Palette documents unification."},{id:"q2",type:"click_correct",question:"Correct the factually incorrect word.",sentence:"The Great Pyramid of Giza was built in Rome as a tomb.",tokens:["The","Great","Pyramid","of","Giza","was","built","in","Rome","as","a","tomb."],incorrectIndex:8,correctAnswers:["Giza","Egypt"],